Learner Track Management

(Core Java | Menu-Based Console Application)

Project Overview

Learner Track Management is a menu-based console application developed using Core Java concepts.
The application allows users to manage Students, Courses, and Enrollments through an interactive command-line menu.

The system demonstrates the use of:

Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)

Layered architecture

In-memory data handling

Business rule validation

Core Entities

The application is built around the following main classes:

Student – Represents a learner in the system

Course – Represents a course that can be offered

Enrollment – Represents the association between a student and a course

Application Flow

The user is prompted with menu options on the console.

Based on the selected option, the user can:

Add a new student

View the list of students

Deactivate a student (soft delete using status)

Add a new course

View the list of courses

Deactivate a course

Enroll a student into a course

View enrollment details

All data is stored in memory using Java collections.